From de388c32f8d167aa377cd4a2e555dc57a4bec1e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 23:32:17 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] fix(sim,motion): plasma laws judge corner hits and
 collinear rings; inside corners keep their tip

Review of #791:

- Tip-up: a rapid in or out of a freed part through one of its corners
  never crossed an edge properly, so it went unjudged. The rapid is now
  split at every contact with the ring (a proper crossing, a vertex it
  passes through, the ends of a stretch along an edge) and judged piece
  by piece: a piece whose midpoint lies strictly inside the part is a
  tip-up. A rapid leaving the part's own edge outward stays clear.
- Cut crossing: two overlapping rings meeting only at vertices or along
  collinear edges never crossed properly and only the torch-height
  warning fired. A later ring with a piece strictly inside the earlier
  ring and one strictly outside it is now refused; a shared edge with
  nothing entering (common-line cutting) stays legal.
- Cover law: every inside corner leaves a kerf-radius tip the torch
  cannot reach, so the law exempts each inside corner's tip zone -
  r (tan(delta/2) - sqrt 3) along each wall, what even the ideal miter
  path leaves beyond 2r; empty from 60 degrees up - and judges only the
  material beyond it. Sharp V-notches generate; the 1 mm notch and
  keyway are still refused, and the refusal names the gap it measured
  against the kerf.

Pinned by sim plasma_laws::a_rapid_through_a_freed_parts_corner_is_a_tip_up,
plasma_laws::an_overlapping_ring_meeting_only_at_vertices_and_edges_is_refused
and motion plasma::tests::a_sharp_inside_corner_generates_with_its_tip_left_not_refused.

Refs #672

