From 873c76b4d34b7bc45b118ca207332a58f42e9e1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 01:27:58 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] fix(sim,motion,app): plasma laws judge hole slugs and the
 reverse crossing; refuse a zero-width slit

- Tip-up: a rapid over an earlier hole's slug is a TipUp naming the
  hole (slug: true), every slug size; the first stretch of the rapid
  leaving the hole just cut is its departure and is not judged.
- Cut crossing: when the later cut is an OUTER contour, an earlier ring
  with a stretch strictly inside it that it does not enclose is refused
  (L cut, then E around it); INNER nesting and common lines unchanged.
- Generation: a picked contour whose zero-width slit Region::new drops
  is refused by name and place, not cut as the plain outline.
- plasma_gate pins an inch document (clean line, a refusal placed in
  inches) and a G41/G42 program judged on its torch-centre rings.
- The vacuous diamond-hole pin is replaced by a nested part touching its
  hole's wall, cut first; decision 4a states the 2r cap refuses
  normal-sized V-notches sharper than about 30 degrees (pinned).

Fixes #801

